{"slug":"container-with-most-water","title":"Container With Most Water","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"medium","order":146,"tags":["arrays","two-pointers","greedy"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Move the shorter wall","body":["Two vertical walls of heights `h[i]` and `h[j]` hold an amount of water equal to `min(h[i], h[j]) * (j - i)`. Start with the widest pair, the first and the last wall. To get a bigger area you must find a taller **shorter wall**, because the width can only shrink.",{"code":"l, r = 0, n - 1\nwhile l < r:\n    best = max(best, min(h[l], h[r]) * (r - l))\n    if h[l] < h[r]: l += 1\n    else: r -= 1"},"Moving the taller wall inward can never help: the height is limited by the shorter wall and the width gets smaller. So we always move the shorter one, and no better pair is skipped."]},"statement":["There are `n` vertical walls standing at the positions 1, 2, ..., n with the given heights. Choose two walls; together with the ground they form a container whose area is the distance between the walls times the height of the shorter wall. Print the largest possible area."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`.","The second line has the `n` heights."],"outputFormat":["Print the largest area."],"constraints":["2 <= n <= 20000","0 <= each height <= 10^4"],"examples":[{"input":"9\n1 8 6 2 5 4 8 3 7\n","output":"49\n","note":"The walls of height 8 (position 2) and 7 (position 9) give 7 * 7 = 49."}],"hints":["The widest container is formed by the first and the last wall.","Its area is limited by the shorter wall, so moving the taller one inward cannot help.","Move the pointer of the shorter wall and keep the best area."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn = int(input())\nh = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> h(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> h[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[] h = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < h.length; i++) h[i] = Long.parseLong(next());\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["Starting from the widest pair, always discard the shorter wall: any container using it with a narrower partner is not better than the one just measured."],"complexity":"Time O(n), space O(1).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn = int(input())\nh = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nl, rr = 0, n - 1\nbest = 0\nwhile l < rr:\n    best = max(best, min(h[l], h[rr]) * (rr - l))\n    if h[l] < h[rr]:\n        l += 1\n    else:\n        rr -= 1\nprint(best)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> h(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> h[i];\n\n    int l = 0, rr = n - 1;\n    long long best = 0;\n    while (l < rr) {\n        best = max(best, min(h[l], h[rr]) * (rr - l));\n        if (h[l] < h[rr]) l++;\n        else rr--;\n    }\n    cout << best << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[] h = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < h.length; i++) h[i] = Long.parseLong(next());\n\n        int l = 0, rr = (int) n - 1;\n        long best = 0;\n        while (l < rr) {\n            best = Math.max(best, Math.min(h[l], h[rr]) * (rr - l));\n            if (h[l] < h[rr]) l++;\n            else rr--;\n        }\n        System.out.println(best);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"9\n1 8 6 2 5 4 8 3 7\n","output":"49\n"},{"input":"2\n1 1\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"2\n0 5\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"5\n5 5 5 5 5\n","output":"20\n"},{"input":"12\n9 9 17 18 9 19 8 19 3 12 8 8\n","output":"88\n"},{"input":"300\n6195 2647 6274 6092 616 2651 9927 6724 8824 3964 1895 6936 5897 2694 9565 2761 6469 8796 7308 6725 6842 3953 605 9867 2062 553 8857 8324 2270 3279 3892 2042 9895 5860 6128 8164 1401 4615 7428 2747 3257 4628 6680 775 6110 4167 5255 228 8850 8215 4625 2573 6341 9842 8816 6420 1395 2535 2382 6211 4557 1632 1961 882 5858 2416 9417 8117 5046 4769 6403 6327 7308 4770 97 9079 2782 7414 9902 3033 4156 9688 2954 1783 3945 8081 7183 3712 457 2868 5492 3200 5355 8408 4287 7814 9091 4447 4434 4497 4635 2347 5373 4180 1826 2328 1858 1661 4814 5914 4244 7053 2353 3742 4606 2204 2245 304 9308 8680 2736 1882 3456 3087 2928 4954 2475 8569 1901 3110 6986 3770 9886 5834 3664 4564 7915 3126 619 4342 1778 5339 7918 769 9370 6804 6616 30 4365 3733 3562 5954 8178 1486 8096 566 7083 4493 3466 1257 9311 1673 1901 752 9025 7178 7417 1364 611 691 2254 9484 5615 4927 8884 9729 8666 7910 5287 3774 3197 2704 7245 1670 1204 7120 6947 7578 74